<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="52002" href="schedule/2019/spring/CMN/538/52002.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="CMN" href="schedule/2019/spring/CMN.xml">Communication</subject><course id="538" href="schedule/2019/spring/CMN/538.xml">Seminar Rhetorical Theory</course></parents><sectionNumber>CF </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Sight, Sound, and Sense</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This seminar will explore current rhetorical theory through the organizing trio of sight, sound, and sense. We will read recent rhetorical scholarship that explores rhetoric’s conceptual, historical, and disciplinary relationships to visuality, materiality, and the senses. Students will leave the course with a clearer picture of the key issues animating these vibrant areas of rhetorical inquiry.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S1 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>4103</roomNumber><buildingName>Lincoln Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Finnegan" firstName="C">Finnegan, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>